# iOS BLE Technical Summary

## Critical limitation

**`native_app/source_code/` is gitignored and not present in this workspace** (0 files under that path). None of the requested native files exist locally:

| Pattern | Expected path (when source is checked out) |
|---|---|
| `BLE_WAKEUP+*.m` | `native_app/source_code/wearfitpro-master/ios/howear/Component/BLE/` |
| `WKBLEConnection*` | `native_app/source_code/phancy-sdk/IwBluetooth/Classes/IwBluetooth/WKBLEConnection/` |
| `BLE_WAKEUP+Glasses.m` | `.../Component/BLE/BLE_WAKEUP+Glasses.m` |
| `BLE_WAKEUP+DeviceRecord*` | `.../Component/BLE/BLE_WAKEUP+DeviceRecord.m` |
| `WKInterpretationManager*` | `.../WKASR/WKInterpretationManager.swift` + `phancy-sdk/.../IwAudioInterpretation/WKAIInterpretationManager.swift` |
| Device record UI/logic | `.../howear/Component/DeviceRecord/` |
| MyDevice glasses | `.../howear/Module/MyDevice/SmartGlasses/` |

What follows is from **inventory index + specs + migrated Dart** (aligned to Android `GlassesOrder.kt` and iOS `BLE_WAKEUP+Glasses.m` per the project's own protocol map). Raw native `.m` content cannot be quoted until source is placed locally.

---

## 1. Protocol frame format (0xEA commands)

### Frame layout

```text
[0xEA][0x00][len_lo][0x00][id][subId][payload...]
```

| Field | Index | Value | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Header | 0 | `0xEA` | Fixed |
| Len pad | 1 | `0x00` | Always zero in practice |
| Length | 2 | `len_lo` | **Single length byte** in Dart impl: `payload.length + 3` (id + subId + payload + 1) |
| Pad | 3 | `0x00` | |
| ID | 4 | domain | Glasses main = `0x34`, WiFi = `0x33`, guide = `0x37`, call record = `0x40` |
| subId | 5 | sub-command | See table below |
| payload | 6+ | variable | |

**Write path (native):** iOS `send_BLE_data` / Android `BleOrderManager` → GATT write characteristic.

### Command domains and subIds (glasses `id = 0x34`)

| subId | Android API | iOS API | Payload (from Dart/native map) |
|---|---|---|---|
| `0x01` | `sendAudioMaxTime` / `sendVideoMaxTime` | `ble_sendGlassesRecordTime:` | `[type, maxTime>>8, maxTime&0xFF]` — type 0=video, 1=audio |
| `0x02` | `sendKeyDefine` | `ble_sendGlassesSetKey:` | 15B Android (l2–l5 long-press); iOS 13B (missing l4/l5) |
| `0x03` | `sendVolume` | `ble_sendGlassesVolume:` | `[volume 0–100]` |
| `0x04` | `switchWakeup` | `ble_sendGlassesAudioWakeupSetter:` / `ble_sendGlassesLowPower` | `[0x00\|0x01]` — iOS reuses subId for low-power |
| `0x05` | `syncFileCount` | `ble_sendGlassesSyncFileNum:` | defer (FTP) |
| `0x06` | `sendNavResult` | receive-side | defer |
| `0x08` | `sendMusic` | `ble_sendGlassesMusicFileOperation:` | defer |
| `0x09` | `switchDirection` | Glasses.m packet | `[direction]` 0=landscape, 1=portrait |
| **`0x0A`** | **`queryWearSwitch` / `setWearSwitch`** | **Glasses.m packet** | **Wear detection — payload format not in repo (defer)** |
| `0x0F` | `setHallSwitch` | `ble_sendSetDeviceHallState:` | `[0x00\|0x01]` |
| `0x10` | `setAutoShutdown` | `ble_sendAutoShutdownMode:min:` | `[mode, minute]` mode 0=query, 1=set |
| `0x11` | `sendDeviceControl` | Glasses.m packet | `[type, action]` — see recording below |

### WiFi domain (`id = 0x33`)

| subId | Purpose | Frame |
|---|---|---|
| `0x09` | Open WiFi scan | `[0xEA,0x00,0x04,0x00,0x33,0x09,0x00]` |
| `0x0C` | Close WiFi scan | `[0xEA,0x00,0x03,0x00,0x33,0x0C]` (no payload — asymmetric) |
| `0x0B` | WiFi reconnect | `[0xEA,0x00,0x03,0x00,0x33,0x0B]` (no payload) |

### Other domains

| ID | Android | iOS | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| `0x37` | `sendGuideMode` | — | Guide mode |
| `0x40` | `sendCallRecordControl*` | `BLE_WAKEUP+DeviceRecord` | Call recording control |
| `0x43` | `fileStartCheck` | — | Pre-transfer file check |

### Verified example frames (from tests)

```dart
// Volume 80
[0xEA, 0x00, 0x04, 0x00, 0x34, 0x03, 80]

// Wakeup on
[0xEA, 0x00, 0x04, 0x00, 0x34, 0x04, 0x01]

// Audio record ON (type=2, action=1)
[0xEA, 0x00, 0x05, 0x00, 0x34, 0x11, 0x02, 0x01]

// Audio max time 300s
[0xEA, 0x00, 0x06, 0x00, 0x34, 0x01, 0x01, 0x01, 0x2C]
```

