## 6. GATT service/characteristic UUIDs

### Default (思澈 / WearfitPro-style, Nordic UART compatible)

Aligned with Android `BleUUID.WATCH_*` and iOS `WKServiceBTConstants`:

| Role | UUID |
|---|---|
| Service | `6e400001-b5a3-f393-e0a9-e50e24dcca9e` |
| Write (commands) | `6e400002-b5a3-f393-e0a9-e50e24dcca9e` |
| Notify (responses) | `6e400003-b5a3-f393-e0a9-e50e24dcca9e` |

**Chip caveat (ADR-0004):** JL (`WKBLEJL` / `WKJLSDK`) and BK (`WKBKSmartGlasses` / `BKSmartCameraKit`) use **different UUIDs and packet paths**. Inventory explicitly says UUIDs vary by chip and are not expanded in the protocol map.

---

## 7. WKInterpretationManager (BLE-adjacent)

Not a BLE protocol file — **WebSocket ASR**, but coordinates with BLE recording:

| Native file | Role |
|---|---|
| `WKInterpretationManager.swift` | WebSocket + audio frame send |
| `WKAIInterpretationManager.swift` (phancy-sdk) | Session coordination, **BLE recording state sync** |

Flutter mirrors: WebSocket to `wss://ai-cloud-hk.4paradigm.com/.../simult_interpretation_auto`, plus `GlassesCommandSender.setRecording` on start/stop; auto-stops on BLE disconnect.

